{"title":"1960 AHSME Problems/Problem 38","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME_Problems/Problem_38&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In this diagram <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> are the equal sides of an isosceles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />, in which is inscribed equilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/2/872e3b09425c9659d782119a543dc858aa520a40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle DEF$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" />. \nDesignate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/d/eed6106eb0d2f3ae22644d7dcd663d4dd7054b71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BFD$\" width=\"57\" height=\"12\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/0/a009564c26bf86933bd2d32bf0c1b854d12a3084.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ADE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"58\" height=\"14\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/f/3af4c3e3ce923bf9084000d50c57eb97365ad5c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle FEC$\" width=\"55\" height=\"12\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />. Then:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/6/2e68e9803a692e34ec8a107038160d6ddd04d072.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(150); defaultpen(linewidth(0.8)+fontsize(10)); pair A=(5,12),B=origin,C=(10,0),D=(5/3,4),E=(10-5*.45,12*.45),F=(6,0); draw(A--B--C--cycle^^D--E--F--cycle); draw(anglemark(E,D,A,1,45)^^anglemark(F,E,C,1,45)^^anglemark(D,F,B,1,45)); label(&quot;$b$&quot;,(D.x+.2,D.y+.25),dir(30)); label(&quot;$c$&quot;,(E.x,E.y-.4),S); label(&quot;$a$&quot;,(F.x-.4,F.y+.1),dir(150)); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,N); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,S); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,S); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,D,dir(150)); label(&quot;$E$&quot;,E,dir(60)); label(&quot;$F$&quot;,F,S);[/asy]\" width=\"198\" height=\"252\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/5/6d5f213825233067ae65bab8a700c5dc305afe10.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ b=\\frac{a+c}{2}\\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ b=\\frac{a-c}{2}\\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ a=\\frac{b-c}{2} \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ a=\\frac{b+c}{2}\\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ \\text{none of these}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"702\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME_Problems/Problem_38&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/2/872e3b09425c9659d782119a543dc858aa520a40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle DEF$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> is an <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Equilateral_triangle\" title=\"Equilateral triangle\">equilateral triangle</a>, all of the angles are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/d/08d5c45388de5c75af641c046d466de3592ffa98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60^{\\circ}$\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" />.\nThe angles in a line add up to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/0/3f0cd95f95238159d02dbcea0aca632c2928991c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"37\" height=\"15\" />, so\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/0/f906f3217b7d85f368079d30a6791c6bc913b48f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle FDB = 120 - b\\]\" width=\"138\" height=\"13\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/9/369cc3ddb9659b584aa501542fd9aff4f751a02a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle EFC = 120 - a\\]\" width=\"138\" height=\"13\" />\nThe angles in a triangle add up to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/0/3f0cd95f95238159d02dbcea0aca632c2928991c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"37\" height=\"15\" />, so\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/d/37dd873d9acdd4d48d13a590755ab9c65c305f23.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle ABC = 60 + b - a\\]\" width=\"159\" height=\"14\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/5/2f567e7ae36f0681c68db3061bafc9a849ed6632.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle ACB = 60 - c + a\\]\" width=\"159\" height=\"14\" />\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> is <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Isosceles_triangle\" title=\"Isosceles triangle\">isosceles</a> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/a/f3ac37c9fa391eebb9601bfaca8bfbfaabdf5ca1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = AC$\" width=\"80\" height=\"13\" />, by Base-Angle Theorem,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/c/68c8273ed912686cc1d39ce96f5157a9d756f624.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[60 + b - a = 60 - c + a\\]\" width=\"184\" height=\"14\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/1/8214d332a19c109702273cad165294b38ae683bb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[b + c = 2a\\]\" width=\"80\" height=\"14\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/2/8d236c2613875652a8908cad3f60bec7c28ea35b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a = \\frac{b+c}{2}\\]\" width=\"73\" height=\"37\" />\nThe answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/3/693c4044f8526a8179956e8ac7a3f2f9d61e2c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"43\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME_Problems/Problem_38&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/ZdM2ou5Gsuw?t=230\">https://youtu.be/ZdM2ou5Gsuw?t=230</a>\n</p><p>~MathProblemSolvingSkills.com\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME_Problems/Problem_38&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME\" title=\"1960 AHSME\">1960 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1960 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1960 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1960\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME_Problems/Problem_37\" title=\"1960 AHSME Problems/Problem 37\">Problem 37</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME_Problems/Problem_39\" title=\"1960 AHSME Problems/Problem 39\">Problem 39</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1960 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wi